Subject: [PATCH] UVM: keep PM VA-list traversal in the existing lock hierarchy

The global PM write lock already excludes every VA-list add/remove and pins
VA lifetimes until resume. Do not reacquire the list mutex under retained VA
locks. Describe the same-class VA collection under that real outer PM lock
with Linux nesting primitives. Keep VMA exclusion and Linux Lockdep enabled.

The existing same-task suspend/resume ownership contract remains required;
the maintained NVIDIA PM worker correction provides it for kernel notifiers.
Audit: creation is inside uvm_unlocked_ioctl()'s PM read grant; destruction is
inside uvm_release_va_space()/uvm_release_deferred()'s PM read grant. The test
VA-list traversal in uvm_va_space_mm.c is read-only.

--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_global.c
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@
     uvm_mutex_lock(&g_uvm_global.va_spaces.lock);
 
     list_for_each_entry(va_space, &g_uvm_global.va_spaces.list, list_node)
-        uvm_va_space_down_write(va_space);
+        uvm_va_space_down_write_pm(va_space, &g_uvm_global.pm.lock);
 
     uvm_mutex_unlock(&g_uvm_global.va_spaces.lock);
 
@@ -380,13 +380,13 @@
     // expectations, so lock tracking is disabled.
     uvm_thread_context_lock_disable_tracking();
 
-    // Release each VA space's lock.
-    uvm_mutex_lock(&g_uvm_global.va_spaces.lock);
-
+    // All list additions and removals require pm.lock in read mode, so its
+    // retained write ownership freezes list membership and VA lifetimes.
+    // Reacquiring the list mutex while the VA locks are held inverts the
+    // normal list -> VA hierarchy. The PM write lock is sufficient here.
+    uvm_assert_rwsem_locked_write(&g_uvm_global.pm.lock);
     list_for_each_entry(va_space, &g_uvm_global.va_spaces.list, list_node)
         uvm_va_space_up_write(va_space);
-
-    uvm_mutex_unlock(&g_uvm_global.va_spaces.lock);
 
     // pm.lock is held in lieu of global_lock to prevent GPU addition/removal
     for_each_gpu_id_in_mask(gpu_id, &g_uvm_global.retained_gpus) {
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_va_space.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_va_space.h
@@ -447,6 +447,21 @@
         uvm_down_write(&(__va_space)->lock);                            \
     } while (0)
 
+// System PM freezes VA list membership with the global PM write lock, then
+// acquires the whole collection of same-class VA locks. That write lock is
+// retained until resume has released all inner locks, and is the nesting
+// lock for this collection. UVM cross-callback tracking is already disabled.
+#define uvm_va_space_down_write_pm(__va_space, __pm_lock)                          \
+    do {                                                                          \
+        uvm_assert_mutex_interrupts();                                            \
+        uvm_assert_rwsem_locked_write(__pm_lock);                                  \
+        mutex_lock_nest_lock(&(__va_space)->serialize_writers_lock.m,              \
+                             &(__pm_lock)->sem);                                   \
+        mutex_lock_nest_lock(&(__va_space)->read_acquire_write_release_lock.m,     \
+                             &(__pm_lock)->sem);                                   \
+        down_write_nest_lock(&(__va_space)->lock.sem, &(__pm_lock)->sem);           \
+    } while (0)
+
 #define uvm_va_space_up_write(__va_space)                                   \
     do {                                                                    \
         uvm_up_write(&(__va_space)->lock);                                  \
